# CLAUDE.local.md — Personal Project Overrides
#
# PURPOSE:
#   This file is your personal Claude Code configuration for the App Gateway
#   Service. It is gitignored and never committed — it is yours alone.
#   Use it to add personal preferences, local environment quirks, or shortcuts
#   that are specific to your machine without polluting the shared CLAUDE.md.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file: cp CLAUDE.local.md.example CLAUDE.local.md
#   2. Edit CLAUDE.local.md with your personal settings
#   3. CLAUDE.local.md will be loaded automatically alongside CLAUDE.md
#
# WHAT BELONGS HERE vs CLAUDE.md:
#   ✅ Here: Personal tool paths, local dev shortcuts, your preferred verbosity level
#   ✅ Here: Local Postgres/Redis connection quirks, your Docker Compose notes
#   ✅ Here: Personal prompt style preferences ("be concise", "explain tradeoffs")
#   ❌ Not here: Team conventions, project architecture, DoD criteria (those live in CLAUDE.md)
#   ❌ Not here: Secrets or credentials (never in any CLAUDE file)
#
# ---

## Personal Environment

# Uncomment and adjust to match your local setup:
# My local API runs on port 3001 (not the default 3000) due to a port conflict.

# My database and Redis are running via Docker Compose. To reset them locally:
# docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml down -v && docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d

# After a reset, re-run migrations and seed a dev user:
# npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed

## Personal Preferences

# Preferred response style:
# - I prefer concise answers. Explain the why, skip obvious steps.
# - When generating tests, show the test first, then ask if I want the implementation.
# - When you find multiple approaches, list them with tradeoffs rather than picking one.

## Local Tool Paths

# If you have non-standard tool installations, document them here:
# Using nvm — Node version is pinned in .nvmrc (if present). Run `nvm use` if you see version errors.
# JWT dev keys: generated locally at tests/fixtures/keys/ — regenerate with [command] if rotated.

